Lab 04: Flexbox, Grid and the JavaScript Runtime and DOM

An office-hours page where a visitor can select a booking slot. It covers two CSS layout engines (Flexbox and Grid) and JavaScript modules, DOM manipulation and the browser runtime.

Features
Flexbox header (title left, navigation right), navigation row and an icon beside its caption
Grid two-column Office Hours section (2fr 1fr) and a two-column feedback form
Responsive layout: one media query switches both grids to a single column at 40rem or narrower
ES modules: main.js imports delay and makeCounter from utils.js
DOM with a single delegated click listener using closest(), dataset, classList.toggle() and querySelectorAll
Async/await booking: the status says "Updating…", waits one second, then confirms with a numbered booking
Accessible: buttons have accessible names, the status paragraph is a live region (role="status"), and booking works from the keyboard
